<div class="view" id="view-configs">
  <div id="storerev">
    <div id="storerevhead">
      <b>store review</b>
      <span class="cfgmut" id="storerevmeta">auto-learned entries awaiting owner review</span>
      <button class="chip" id="storerevReload" style="margin-left:auto">↻ reload</button>
    </div>
    <div id="storerevlist"><div class="empty">open the configs tab to load the review queue…</div></div>
  </div>
  <div id="cfgbar">
    <input id="cfgFilter" placeholder="filter cwd / config…" autocomplete="off">
    <span class="chip on" data-ch="all">all</span>
    <span class="chip" data-ch="claude">claude</span>
    <span class="chip" data-ch="codex">codex</span>
    <span id="cfgStatus" class="cfgmut"></span>
    <button class="chip" id="cfgReload" style="margin-left:auto">↻ rescan</button>
  </div>
  <div id="cfgsplit">
    <div id="cfgtree"><div class="empty">open the configs tab to scan…</div></div>
    <div class="raildrag" id="cfgraildrag" title="drag to resize — double-click resets"></div>
    <div id="cfgdetail"><div class="empty">pick a cwd or a home to see what its agents load →</div></div>
  </div>
  <!-- GUARD REFUSALS, AND THE OWNER'S DIAL (moved here from the Work page,
       task/3445: the fleet's own machinery sits with its configs). How often a guard stopped an
       agent this week (`helm friction`'s own numbers), and the one number
       that decides when an agent is told it may stop and repair a guard. It
       sits beside readiness because both answer "is the fleet's own machinery
       getting in its way", and it is a control he turns here because he does
       not type verbs. It boots saying "Not read yet", and an unreadable
       record is never drawn as zero refusals. -->
  <section id="frictionsec"></section>
  <!-- THE STORE COUNTS AND THE SKILLS (moved here from the Work page,
       task/3445): what the fleet has learned and can load, beside the configs
       that load it. -->
  <section id="store"></section>
  <section id="skillsec"></section>
</div>
